## Blocking finding

**P2 — Class type parameters named org do not prevent qualified annotation
confirmation** (android_junit4_declarations.rs, line 1039; confirmation at
line 1211). The class-header pass includes Test in its shadowing checks but
omits org. Qualified confirmation checks declared/imported org names and
inherited scope, but neither of the following owners has a declared supertype:

~~~java
class Suite<org> {
  @org.junit.Test public void actual() {}
}
~~~

~~~kotlin
class Suite<org> {
  @org.junit.Test fun actual() {}
}
~~~

The known class type parameter shadows the leading qualifier. These declarations
must retain their source/header/annotation/method facts while leaving that
reference unresolved. Include org class type parameters in prefix-shadowing
analysis, with Java and Kotlin regressions. Preserve the existing generic Test
negative assertion.

This is the new task's second owner fix already reviewed; the next consolidation
is owner fix round 3. Its history remains separate from the prior reference
archive discovery task.

